        "fact-16153655-0"
      ],
      "text": "mtg has taken third on the ARC-AGI-3 public board with 50.37, edging the last dance by 0.52 points. The entry adds 5.37 points since the previous close and improves one place. Its sole listed Kaggle account, michaeltgao, displays the name Michael. The score establishes a new order among the challengers; it does not disclose how the submission achieved it."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Third place changes hands twice",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-16-0805-arc-3-last-dance-climbs-third"
      ],
      "text": "The last dance reached third earlier today, as the wire reported, after improving from 43.64 to 49.85. mtg’s later advance leaves it fourth, still two places higher than at yesterday’s close. Son & Mark & Ronen falls from third to fifth with its score unchanged at 47.25. That is the day’s clearest sporting consequence: two improving rivals have overtaken yesterday’s leading challenger."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The leaders stay clear; the chase gets deeper",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "Tufa Labs remains first at 68.91 and Yi-Chia Chen second at 67.49, both unchanged since the previous close. Even after mtg’s advance, Chen is more than seventeen points ahead of third. Behind the new top five, 復活の混テキスト gains 5.58 points and five places to finish sixth at 45.11. Majkel1337 is seventh at 44.84; its recorded overnight score event adds 2.18 points, while its full close-to-close comparison is unavailable. NVARC3 holds 43.94 but drops from fifth to eighth. Score gains have reshaped the chase without yet narrowing the leading pair’s advantage enough to threaten second place."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The gold line moves beyond the top ten",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "The provisional gold score rises from 37.98 to 38.20. insuperabilehart reaches 26th at 36.73 after gaining 4.65 points, and Zyy7390 climbs from 270th to 29th with a 4.86-point improvement to 36.22. Both make substantial progress while remaining below the gold line. yin reaches 94th at 33.23, up 98 places since the previous close. These public positions remain provisional; final medals are still open."
    },
